=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_3f7d — Entry hook is a morning landing pad, sorted by evening (fork of p_b2c8)

The parent document p_b2c8 held that the entry area is a permanent chaos zone: Yuki's laptop, notebook, and water bottle pile up on the entry hook and stay there until a Sunday reset. Six evening looks at the entry hook found neither the laptop nor the notebook, refuting the "permanent chaos" thesis. What the evidence supports instead is a *transient* drop: Yuki's things land at the entry hook when she arrives from work (around 17:30) or when she's grabbing them to leave in the morning, but by the time the evening patrols run (18:00–22:00) she has sorted them to their proper homes. The laptop and notebook go to the office desk; the water bottle goes to the kitchen table where she drinks from it in the evening.

This hypothesis predicts that the entry hook will be *empty* of Yuki's personal items during the 18:00–22:00 window on weekdays, and that the office desk (desk_o1) will hold the laptop and notebook in that same window. It differs from p_b2c8 in that the chaos is a 30-minute morning/afternoon blip, not an all-week state. It differs from p_c3d4 (which puts the laptop at the office desk only on WFH days) in that Yuki brings her laptop home every evening and works from the office desk even on office days for personal tasks or journaling prep.

What would refute this: a look at the entry hook during 18:00–22:00 that finds the laptop or notebook still there, or a look at the office desk in that window that finds neither.

