=== HYPOTHESIS ===
# p_8c2a — Kitchen-table dinner, minimal prep, no formal dining (fork of p_c007)

The parent document p_c007 predicted a shared dinner-cooking ritual: cutting board and pan deployed on the kitchen counter, plates set at the dining table, 18:00–19:30. The evidence refutes all three: nine looks found no pan at the counter during that window, seven found no cutting board, and two found no plates at the dining table. Yet Yuki was sighted in the kitchen at 18:00 on a Tuesday, so she *is* making something. The revised picture is that dinner is a quick, informal meal at the kitchen table (kitchen_table_k1), not the formal dining table. The pan stays in the cupboard (no stovetop cooking); the cutting board may be used briefly at the kitchen table for chopping but is not deployed on the main counter. Plates come from the cupboard to the kitchen table, not to the dining table. Omar is at work until 23:00, so this is Yuki eating alone; the "shared" aspect of the parent's title was wrong for the 18:00 window.

This hypothesis predicts that during the 18:00–19:30 weekday window, the kitchen table will hold plates and a mug, the pan will remain in the cupboard, and the dining table will be clear. It differs from p_c007 in location (kitchen table vs. dining table) and in the absence of stovetop cooking. It differs from p_a1b2 (which also puts plates at the dining table) in the same way.

What would refute this: a look at the kitchen table during 18:00–19:30 that finds no plates, or a look at the cupboard that finds the pan has been removed, or a look at the dining table that finds plates set.

